um/general/off-topic/1051006-the-last-jedi?p=1060003#post1060003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Jedi&quot; is both singluar and plural (a Jedi, the jedi) so &quot;The Last Jedi&quot; could very well refer to multiple Jedi rather than a single one (Luke or Rei).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. We have already established this higher up on the thread. In fact, the foreign language titles for the film make it clear that it's intended to be plural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}